== 1. the scan reads every @render_mode, and refuses four shapes ==
ok   default: server
ok   Counter: client
ok   Banner: static
ok   Plain declares nothing: inherit
ok   Late prerender: false
ok   Counter prerender: true
ok   a type that declared nothing prerenders: true
ok   a misspelled mode is not applied: inherit
ok   a non-component is not applied: inherit
ok   the misspelling is refused once: 1
ok   the non-component is refused once: 1
ok   browser types: latte$entry.AutoGood,latte$entry.Counter,latte$entry.Late,latte$entry.Unserializable

== 2. precedence: block, then instance, then the type, then around it ==
ok   nothing declared inherits: server
ok   the type wins over what is around it: client
ok   the instance wins over the type: server
ok   a block wins over the instance: static
ok   and says where it came from: @render_mode
ok   an inherited answer says so: application default
ok   equal modes are not a boundary: false
ok   different modes are: true
ok   static inside server is a boundary too: true

== 3. a client component in a server page is one opaque element ==
<main id="page"><latte-boundary data-latte-boundary="1" data-latte-mode="client" data-latte-component="latte$entry.Counter" data-latte-props="{&quot;start&quot;:1,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;board&quot;}" data-latte-prerendered=""><div class="counter"><span>board=1</span><button>+1</button></div></latte-boundary></main>
ok   faults: (none)
0 open latte-boundary
  1 attr data-latte-boundary=1
  2 attr data-latte-mode=client
  3 attr data-latte-component=latte$entry.Counter
  4 attr data-latte-props={"start":1,"label":"board"}
  5 flag data-latte-prerendered=true
  6 opaque
  7 raw <div class="counter"><span>board=1</span><button>+1</button></div>
/close

== 4. a prop change is one attribute edit, and nothing inside ==
ok   one prop changed: #1 in 0 | #1 attr 4:data-latte-props = {"start":42,"label":"board"} | #1 out
ok   the prerendered body is untouched: true
ok   an unchanged render: (nothing)

== 5. a static region has no instance, and its HTML is its props ==
<main id="page"><latte-boundary data-latte-boundary="1" data-latte-mode="static" data-latte-component="latte$entry.Banner" data-latte-props="{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;board&quot;}" data-latte-prerendered=""><h2>board</h2></latte-boundary></main>
ok   a static region re-renders from its props: #1 in 0 | #1 attr 4:data-latte-props = {"title":"counter"} | #1 markup 0 = <h2>counter</h2> | #1 out

== 6. prerender: false leaves the element empty ==
<main id="page"><latte-boundary data-latte-boundary="1" data-latte-mode="client" data-latte-component="latte$entry.Late" data-latte-props="{&quot;note&quot;:&quot;board&quot;}"></latte-boundary></main>
ok   faults: (none)

== 7. what a boundary refuses, at the boundary, by name ==
ok   a List parameter cannot cross: latte$entry.Unserializable.rows is a @param of type List<string>, which cannot cross an execution boundary; a prop is a string, an int, a bool or a float. A callback across a boundary is a server action, not a closure
  1: latte$entry.DeadButton is rendered static and binds on:click; a static region has no instance, so the handler can never run
ok   a misspelled render:mode is refused with the word in it: true

== 8. an application that declares no mode renders the same bytes ==
ok   no scan: <main id="page"><em>board</em></main>
ok   a scan that knows about other types changes nothing: <main id="page"><em>board</em></main>
ok   and mounts the same number of components: 2=2
ok   render:mode on an undeclared component makes a boundary: true

== 9. opaque stops the differ at the element, attributes and all ==
ok   an opaque element sends its attributes and nothing inside: #0 in 0 | #0 attr 1:data-x = b | #0 out
ok   and without the mark the same change reaches the child: #0 in 0 | #0 attr 1:data-x = b | #0 text 0 = b | #0 out

