== 11. auto is a decision between the two runtimes, taken once ==
ok   with no bundle, an auto component is not a boundary: <main id="page"><b>3</b></main>
ok   and nothing in the page says client: false
ok   with a bundle, the same component is a client region: true
ok   carrying its props: true
ok   and its server render inside it, to paint before the bundle runs: true
ok   a re-render does not move a mounted region: true

== 12. the four nestings, and the one that is refused ==
ok   a static region inside a client one renders: <div class="inner">a<latte-boundary data-latte-boundary="1" data-latte-mode="static" data-latte-component="latte$entry.Banner" data-latte-props="{&quot;title&quot;:&quot;a&quot;}" data-latte-prerendered=""><h2>a</h2></latte-boundary></div>
ok   and nothing about it is foreign: (none)
ok   a static region inside a client one follows its props: #0 in 0 | #0 text 0 = b | #0 out | #1 in 0 | #1 attr 4:data-latte-props = {"title":"b"} | #1 markup 0 = <h2>b</h2> | #1 out
ok   a client region inside a client one is no boundary at all: false
ok   it is just a child: <div class="inner">c<div class="counter"><span>c=0</span><button>+1</button></div></div>
ok   a component can ask where it is running: client
ok   and so can everything the same renderer holds: client/client
ok   a static render says so: static
ok   a server region inside a client one is refused: 0: <Plain> at 4 resolves to server inside a client region; a server region inside a browser one needs a server mount protocol latte does not have yet. Move it out of the client region, or make it client
ok   and the component renders where it is, rather than vanishing: <main id="page"><em>board</em></main>

78 checks, 0 bad
